<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of Guadeloupe</h1><p class="st-meta">1635 CE – 1946 CE · capital Basse-Terre</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">French sugar colony in the Lesser Antilles, where slavery was abolished, restored and abolished again, now an overseas department of France.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-lienard-de-lolive">Charles Liénard de l'Olive</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-du-plessis-dossonville">Jean du Plessis d'Ossonville</a> landed in 1635 for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/compagnie-des-iles-de-lamerique">Compagnie des Îles d'Amérique</a>. Settlers fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinago">Kalinago</a>, who were driven off within a few decades. The colony passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-west-india-company">French West India Company</a> in 1664 and then to the crown in 1674.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A royal governor ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basse-terre">Basse-Terre</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pointe-a-pitre">Pointe-à-Pitre</a> grew into the main commercial port. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">Sugar plantations</a> worked by enslaved Africans dominated the economy, regulated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/code-noir">Code Noir</a> of 1685. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> occupied the island in 1759 to 1763 and again in later wars. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">Revolution</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-hugues">Victor Hugues</a> abolished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in 1794, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> restored it in 1802, crushing the resistance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-delgres">Louis Delgrès</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">Slavery</a> was finally abolished in 1848 through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-schoelcher">Victor Schoelcher's</a> decree, after which indentured workers came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. A law of 19 March 1946 made Guadeloupe an overseas <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, ending its colonial status; it remains a French department and region today.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1635 CE – 1946 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.24%;width:6.19%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1635 CE – 1946 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Basse-Terre</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Charles Liénard de l'Olive, Victor Hugues</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French and Guadeloupean Creole</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>French Guadeloupe, Guadeloupe</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1790&amp;focus=colony-of-guadeloupe" aria-label="Colony of Guadeloupe on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2997 1583 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of Guadeloupe lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3317 1839L5054 728M3317 1839L3317 1839"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M3317 1839h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3317 1839h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3317 1839h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Basse-Terre. <a href="/atlas?year=1790&amp;focus=colony-of-guadeloupe">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
